Subject: [PATCH 3/7] codex-swapper mod: OpenCode Go key failover on usage
 exhaustion

When the opencode-go gateway rejects a request with 401/402/403/429, rotate
the preferred key in $CODEX_HOME/oc-go.key (1 <-> 2), refresh the external
auth command, and retry exactly once. The provider is matched by its base
URL so no other provider path is touched, and a user pin in
$CODEX_HOME/oc-go.override disables rotation.

The key value itself is resolved by ~/.codex/bin/oc-go-key, which reads the
state file and prints the matching Keychain secret (opencode-go /
opencode-go-alt), falling back to the other key when the selected item is
missing or empty.

